and JavaScript are popular general-purpose 
 programming languages that are widely used for various applications. 
 While they share some similarities, each language has distinct features, 
 development environments, and associated costs. Choosing the best 
 language depends on factors like the project's scope, intended audience, 
 and desired outcomes. Even then, no single language excels at every task. 
 As a result, programmers often select a language that balances performance, 
 simplicity, and adaptability to meet the demands of their project. 
 Ultimately, becoming proficient in one or more programming languages takes 
 time and practice, with the journey being just as educational as the 
 destination. The following examples illustrate how the same program can 
 be written in different programming languages to demonstrate their 
 equivalency. The programs are a simple calculator that can perform tasks 
 like adding two numbers together. 
